or a Pung.\n\nSo the answer would be to Play W7.\n</think>\n\nEvaluation: The optimal move is to discard a W7 to preserve the potential for forming two Chows (T2-T3-T4 and B2-B3-B4) and a pair of W7s, which maximizes scoring flexibility. Discarding W7 also avoids giving opponents a chance to complete high-value melds with B2 or W2.\n\nReason: By discarding one W7, the hand retains B2, B3, B4 for a potential B2-B3-B4 Chi, and keeps two W7s for a possible Pung or pair. This setup supports multiple scoring patterns like Mixed Double Pung (2 points) and All Chows (2 points), while minimizing risk of aiding opponents with critical tiles like B2 or W2.\n\nAnswer: Play W7"}
